<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>		   27/11/96		19/12/96	     29/12/95</p>
<p> Gasoline	  425		     400		    425</p>
<p> Naphtha	   100		  75-100		     50</p>
<p> Gas oil	 1,950	   2,050/2,100	  1,575/1,600</p>
<p> Fuel oil    300/325		     350		    325</p>
<p> Jet		  25			25		     10</p>
<p>Mogas inventories were balanced with incoming cargoes just topping barge offtake into Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha saw limited top-up requirements from Petrochemicals but incoming supplies continued to outweigh demand.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were slightly lower with wintry weather drawing good demand from inland markets.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks were also lower with little incoming material to balance offtake into the bunkering sector.</p>
<p>Jet stocks held steady but most incoming material was seen going into the gas oil pool for blending.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7456</p>
</text>
